title: Daemon configuration
tags: Daemon Configuration
kind: reference
summary: daemon/config.toml — the repositories to load at startup, and the [settings] knobs with their defaults.

`~/.config/metafolder/daemon/config.toml` (`--config <path>` overrides it). Not to
be confused with each repository's `config.json` ([[Repository layout on disk]]).

```
[[load]]
root = "/data/music"

[[load]]
metafolder = "/ssd/meta/music/.metafolder"

[settings]
watch-quiet-period-ms = 2000
```

''`[[load]]`'' — the repositories to load at startup, each with exactly one of
`root` or `metafolder`, like a `POST /repos/load` body.

''`[settings]`'' — every key optional:

|!Key |!Default |!Meaning |
|`watch-quiet-period-ms` |`2000` |how long the filesystem must stay quiet before the watcher applies its buffered events ([[Event batching]]) |
|`watch-budget-share` |`50` |the percentage of the kernel's per-user inotify watch limit this daemon allows itself ([[The watch budget]]) |
|`watchd-socket` |`/run/metafolder/watchd.sock` |where the fanotify broker is looked for at load ([[Watch sources and regimes]]): reachable, the tree is covered through it; not, the daemon watches with inotify. A path where nothing listens keeps it on inotify |
|`orphan-cascade-limit` |`10000` |the largest number of metarecords one watcher batch may orphan; beyond, the cascade is skipped with a warning (`0`: no limit; [[Orphan scan]]) |
|`log-retention-revisions` |`200` |revisions of history the event log keeps behind HEAD (`0`: everything); a repository can override it |
|`log-retention-keep-labels` |`true` |whether a labelled revision stops the trim; a repository can override it |
|`slow-operation-threshold-ms`, `slow-read-threshold-ms`, `slow-operation-reads-threshold` |`2000`, `100`, `100000` |[[Slow log configuration]] |
|`auto-backup-days` |`1` |every how many days each loaded repository gets its automatic backup, into `internal/backups/auto/` — one slot, replaced only by a backup that checks clean (`0`: off; [[Backups and restore]]) |

A missing file is an empty one. A malformed one — invalid TOML, an unknown
top-level key, a `[[load]]` entry with both or neither of `root`/`metafolder` —
stops the daemon at startup. An unknown key ''inside `[settings]`'' is ignored, so
that a retired setting does not break every configuration that still carries
it. A repository that fails to load is a warning; the daemon starts anyway, with
the others.
